[size=6][b]DaveDiverExpansion 2.0 [/b][/size]
is an all-in-one quality-of-life mod for [i]Dave the Diver[/i], built on BepInEx 6 (IL2CPP) + HarmonyX (tested with BepInEx 6.0.0-be.752). It keeps the original [b]DaveDiverExpansion[/b] framework — including the in-game [b]F1 settings panel[/b], dive map, auto pickup and iDiver upgrades — and folds in the full [b]SuperDave[/b] feature set (infinite oxygen, toxic aura, infinite drones/traps, speed boosts, weapon hotkeys and more). Everything lives in a single plugin, with one config file and one settings panel.
[size=5][b]Highlights[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]One plugin, one config — no conflicting mods to juggle [/*]
[*]Full in-game settings panel: press [b]F1[/b], every option with a description, rebinding and "Reset All Settings" [/*]
[*]Panel is a collapsible tree grouped into 6 areas: [b]Diving / Farming / Sushi / Map / Automation / System[/b] — hotkeys sit next to the feature they drive [/*]
[*]On-screen [b]status HUD[/b]: Toxic Aura state/mode + common toggles, flashes when the aura is toggled, corner configurable [/*]
[*]Auto pickup fish/items/chests while diving, with a configurable radius and smart filtering [/*]
[*]Full-screen dive map with marker toggles — press [b]M[/b] [/*]
[*]Instant capture: Toxic Aura (kill or sleep), infinite drones & crab traps [/*]
[*][b]Auto Call Drone[/b] — the salvage drone is called for you when you swim up to a downed large fish [/*]
[*]Diving buffs: infinite oxygen, invincible, infinite bullets, weightless items [/*]
[*]Sushi bar: infinite patience, infinite wasabi, money boost [/*]
[*]Weapon hotkeys: heal, give guns, level weapons up/down [/*]
[*]English + 简体中文 interface [/*]
[/list]
All options are off/on individually — install it even if you only want the map or auto pickup.
[line]
[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://builds.bepinex.dev/projects/bepinex_be][b]BepInEx 6 Bleeding Edge[/url] — download the [b]Unity.IL2CPP-win-x64[/b] build. [/*]
[*]Extract BepInEx into your game folder:
[code]Steam/steamapps/common/Dave the Diver/[/code]
[/*]
[*][b]Launch the game once[/b] so BepInEx generates
[code]BepInEx/interop[/code]
, then close it. [/*]
[*]Download
[code]DaveDiverExpansion-2.0.4.zip[/code]
from this page and extract it. [/*]
[*]Copy the
[code]dave-diver-expansion2.0[/code]
folder into:
[code]Dave the Diver/BepInEx/plugins/[/code]
so you end up with
[code]BepInEx/plugins/dave-diver-expansion2.0/dave-diver-expansion2.0.dll[/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch the game and press [b]F1[/b] to open the settings panel. [/*]
[/list]
[b]Updating:[/b] just replace the old
[code]dave-diver-expansion2.0[/code]
folder with the new one. Your settings are kept (
[code]BepInEx/config/com.davediver.expansion2.0.cfg[/code]
). [b]Uninstall:[/b] delete
[code]BepInEx/plugins/dave-diver-expansion2.0/[/code]
(and optionally the config file).
[line]
[size=5][b]Main features[/b][/size] [b]DaveDiverExpansion framework[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Auto Pickup[/b] — automatically collects nearby fish, items and chests while diving
[list]
[*]Configurable pickup radius [/*]
[*]Independent toggles for fish / items / chests / ammo boxes / oxygen boxes [/*]
[*]Smart filtering: skips weapons to prevent swap loops, respects grab-level limits [/*]
[*]Pauses during cutscenes so quests don't break [/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[*][b]Dive Map[/b] — minimap HUD + full map overlay
[list]
[*]Press [b]M[/b] to toggle the enlarged map (scroll to zoom, drag to pan) [/*]
[*]Marker toggles for aggressive fish / ores / chests / escape pods / fish [/*]
[*]Auto-disables in Merfolk Village (it has its own map) [/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[*][b]iDiver Extension[/b] — extra upgrades in the iDiver panel: harpoon damage, movement/booster speed, booster duration, crab trap count/efficiency, drone count, fish density ×2/×3/×4 [/*]
[*][b]Auto Seahorse Race[/b] — auto-controls your seahorse during races [/*]
[*][b]Betting Expansion[/b] — casino bets up to 5000 [/*]
[*][b]Quick Scene Switch[/b] — press [b]F2[/b] to jump between scenes [/*]
[*][b]In-Game Config Panel[/b] — press [b]F1[/b]; live-edit every setting, rebind hotkeys by clicking a row and pressing a key [/*]
[*][b]6-area tree panel[/b] — Diving / Farming / Sushi / Map / Automation / System, with Expand/Collapse All; related hotkeys are listed inside their feature area [/*]
[*][b]Status HUD[/b] — always-on corner overlay showing Toxic Aura state/mode and Infinite Oxygen / Invincible / Infinite Bullets; flashes when the aura is toggled; corner and per-line toggles configurable [/*]
[/list]
[b]SuperDave features[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Diving buffs[/b] — Infinite Oxygen, Invincible, Weightless Items, Infinite Bullets, hide item popups [/*]
[*][b]Infinite Drones[/b] & [b]Infinite Crab Traps[/b] (+ auto-drop traps on trap zones) [/*]
[*][b]Toxic Aura[/b] — insta-kill or sleep fish around Dave, with hotkeys to toggle/switch mode [/*]
[*][b]Speed boosts[/b] — swim, boat walk, farm, fish farm, sushi bar & staff [/*]
[*][b]Sushi bar[/b] — infinite customer patience, infinite wasabi, money boost, faster cooking [/*]
[*][b]Default Harpoon Head[/b] — auto-equip a chosen harpoon type + level on every dive [/*]
[*][b]Weapon hotkeys[/b] — full heal, give Tranq/Net/Snipe gun, weapon level up/down [/*]
[*][b]Auto Call Drone[/b] — automatically call the salvage drone for a large fish the game allows it on when Dave is close (configurable radius); no aiming and no holding the interact key [/*]
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Changelog[/b][/size]
[b]v2.0.4[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] fish in the [b]fish farm[/b] no longer freeze when [b]Weightless Items[/b] is on. The item-weight getters that option patches are byte-for-byte identical to the fish movers' speed getters, and the IL2CPP toolchain folds such identical bodies onto a single shared native function �� so zeroing item weight also zeroed the fish swim / rotation speed. The patch now verifies the object's real runtime type and only zeroes genuine item weights. [/*]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] the dive [b]minimap[/b] no longer overlaps the [b]Merfolk Village[/b] UI. The village is loaded additively, so it is never the active scene and the old "active scene name" check never matched; the mod now scans every loaded scene. [/*]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] reworked infinite patience for sushi-bar customers by freezing the food / drink patience tickers directly, so customers no longer stay stuck at the table and drink orders are no longer wrongly flagged as unsatisfied. [/*]
[*][b]Improved:[/b] verbose diagnostics are now gated behind the [b]DebugLog[/b] option, so the BepInEx log stays clean by default. [/*]
[/list]
[b]v2.0.3[/b]
[list]
[*][b]New:[/b] [b]Auto Call Drone[/b] — the salvage drone is called automatically when Dave swims close to a large fish the game allows the drone on. Replaces the old [i]Large Pickups[/i] option. [/*]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] [b]Dave could get stuck and stop moving entirely[/b] when the old [i]Large Pickups[/i] option was on. It turned big fish into ordinary pickups without a valid pickup command, which made the game hit a null reference every frame in its input callback and freeze the player. Large fish keep their native drone interaction now. [/*]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] the Toxic Aura treated every [b]large[/b] fish as awake — the sleep check read a field that does not exist on the buff handler, so big fish were re-slept over and over and could keep resisting the aura. [/*]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] [b]Infinite Drones[/b] no longer fights the iDiver [i]Drone Count[/i] upgrade (it rewrote the drone count every frame and spammed "overwrite detected"); the count no longer oscillates. [/*]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] fish are no longer registered twice in the internal entity list, so pickup/map/aura features stop doing duplicate work per fish. [/*]
[*][b]Improved:[/b] the settings panel is now a collapsible tree with Expand/Collapse All, so long option lists are much easier to navigate. [/*]
[/list]
[b]v2.0.2[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] [b]Weightless Items[/b] now only applies while the option is on — turning it off restores normal item weights instead of leaving shared item data at zero. [/*]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] farm / fish-farm walk speed changes now apply live instead of only after reloading the farm. [/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] status HUD (bottom-left by default) — aura state/mode plus Infinite Oxygen / Invincible / Infinite Bullets; flashes when the aura is toggled, corner configurable. [/*]
[*][b]Improved:[/b] the F1 panel groups every setting into 6 areas with related hotkeys listed next to the feature they drive. [/*]
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Default hotkeys[/b][/size]
[b]Press directly[/b]
[list]
[*][b]F1[/b] — open / close the settings panel [/*]
[*][b]F2[/b] — open the scene-switch menu [/*]
[*][b]M[/b] — toggle the enlarged dive map [/*]
[/list]
[b]SuperDave hotkeys[/b] (hold the modifier key, default
[code]LeftControl[/code]
, then press the action key):
[list]
[*][b]Modifier[/b] —
[code]LeftControl[/code]
— hold for the hotkeys below; set to [code]None[/code] to use them without a modifier [/*]
[*][b]Toggle Toxic Aura[/b] —
[code]Backspace[/code]
— aura on/off [/*]
[*][b]Aura Mode[/b] —
[code]Backslash[/code]
— Sleep / Kill [/*]
[*][b]Heal[/b] —
[code]Keypad0[/code]
— fully heal Dave [/*]
[*][b]Net Gun[/b] —
[code]Keypad1[/code]
— give a Net Gun [/*]
[*][b]Tranq Gun[/b] —
[code]Keypad2[/code]
— give a Tranq Gun [/*]
[*][b]Sniper[/b] —
[code]Keypad3[/code]
— give a Sniper [/*]
[*][b]Weapon Up[/b] —
[code]KeypadPlus[/code]
— weapon level +1 [/*]
[*][b]Weapon Down[/b] —
[code]KeypadMinus[/code]
— weapon level -1 [/*]
[/list]
[b]Notes:[/b] [code]Backspace[/code] and [code]\[/code] are pressed on their own — no modifier needed. The weapon keys default to the [b]numeric keypad[/b] (not the number row above the letters); on a keyboard without a numpad, rebind them under [b]Diving → Weapon Control[/b]. Every key can be rebound in-game by pressing [b]F1[/b] and clicking the hotkey row. [b]Auto Call Drone[/b] has no hotkey — it triggers on its own.
[line]
[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/1868140/Dave_the_Diver/][b]Dave the Diver[/url] (Steam, current version) [/*]
[*][url=https://builds.bepinex.dev/projects/bepinex_be][b]BepInEx 6 Bleeding Edge[/url] — [i]Unity.IL2CPP-win-x64[/i] build (required, not bundled; tested with 6.0.0-be.752) [/*]
[*]Windows 10/11, x64 [/*]
[*]No other mod dependencies — this is a single standalone plugin [/*]
[/list]
[b]Notes / compatibility[/b]
[list]
[*]This mod bundles the features of the older [i]DaveDiverExpansion[/i] and [i]SuperDave[/i] mods. [b]Do not install those at the same time[/b] — remove them first to avoid duplicate configs and patch conflicts. [/*]
[*]Save your game before enabling the more powerful options (infinite oxygen, toxic aura, etc.). [/*]
[*]Single-player only. [/*]
[*]If the game updates and a feature breaks, check the mod page for a new release. [/*]
[/list]

